{%- comment -%}
  Canonical adult size chart rows (cm), shared by:
  - sections/size-guide.liquid (standalone size guide page)
  - snippets/variant-main-picker.liquid (PDP "SIZE GUIDE" drawer)

  Source: merchant workbook Sheet1!B1:T5, supplied 2026-10-29 (CM).
  Confirmed mapping: 00 -> 00; 02-16 -> 2-16; 18-30 -> 18W-30W.
  Extra source sizes 0, 16W and 32W are intentionally omitted.

  Each row is size|bust|waist|hips|hollow-to-hem in centimeters.
  Pass unit: 'in' for initial inch values, and row_headers: true for row headers.
  Both consumers use data-cm to switch units without rounding the source values.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture chart -%}
00|79|61|88.5|145
02|84|66|93.5|147
04|86.5|68.5|96|147
06|89|71|98.5|150
08|91.5|73.5|101|150
10|94|76|104|152
12|96.5|80|108|152
14|100.5|84|112|155
16|104|87.5|116|155
18|116|99|125|155
20|121|105|130|155
22|126|111|135|155
24|131|117|140|155
26|136|123|145|155
28|141|128|150|155
30|147.5|135|157|155
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign rows = chart | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
{%- for row in rows -%}
  {%- assign values = row | strip | split: '|' -%}
  <tr>
    {%- if row_headers -%}
      <th scope="row">{{ values.first }}</th>
    {%- else -%}
      <td>{{ values.first }}</td>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- for cm in values offset: 1 -%}
      <td data-cm="{{ cm }}">
        {%- if unit == 'in' -%}
          {{- cm | divided_by: 2.54 | round: 1 | append: '' | remove: '.0' -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- cm -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </td>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </tr>
{%- endfor -%}
